ou in your successes in chess  and certainly are looking to uh to watch  you as you as you go further  uh with chess nationally and  internationally as well  so i wish you all the very very best but  to all the guests that are here from out  of town  um it's always a thrill to have you here  and as i said uh with this quality  organization  uh we're very very proud to uh be  uh you know really a player nationally  and and internationally in the chess  world  and we want to continue to be so thank  you genie uh and thank you rex and  certainly  look forward to some more great events  in the future  thank you thank you mr mayor there are  so many people to thank i don't know  where to begin but i have to begin  somewhere  so first of all did we not have the best  commentators in the history of chess  and then to joy bray and tony rich and  all of their associates they did an  amazing  job organizing and running this event  thank you so much  all of you  and i of course especially want to thank  the players  and for being so accommodating of all of  your fans  you know that's quite a burden the way  they crowd you but i saw how generously  you gave  of your time and we thank you very much  for that  uh how ironic in this city which all  americans know is the greatest sports  city  in the united states it has it has that  name  and next door at leicester's the best  sports bar in saint louis  yesterday the manager said he has never  seen the place so full  and what caused it but not a football or  baseball game but a chess match  what a wonderful thing and i'm also  delighted that  magnus and lavonne got to go to a  baseball game and i hope you understand  how important it is  that you go back to your countries and  tell your governments that baseball  should be your national sport  so jeannie you will come up we'll  present the  trophy  so magnus carlson  our honor and privilege to present you  with this first single field cup  congratulations  okay yeah thank you okay thank you like  to say a couple words  here so you can talk no  um  i don't have too much time i'd like to  thank uh rex  and and and ginny uh again  uh for uh for a wonderful tournament and  um  if everything uh goes well i'll be uh  i'll be back  yes thank you i will say now that you've  been to st  louis you know where it is and you know  how to get here we expect you to come  back frequently and lavon also  and uh just one more thing i uh  i um i do not necessarily uh  agree on the whole uh whole baseball  thing  um but it's always interesting to see a  game that  resembles chess at least a little bit  so as i alluded to before make sure you  stay tuned for  uh uh maybe 11 months or so from now  um i am proud to announce to you that we  will be hosting the  2014 sink field cup here at the chess  club and scholastic center as well  so in closing i would like to thank you  all once again for joining us  i'm sure that the players have enjoyed  seeing all of their fans and all of the  reporters  and making sure that the brilliancies  that they have  have demonstrated over the chessboard  have reached the masses  i want to thank all of our spectators  obviously it's because of you that the  event was so successful there's a real  electricity in the air real  uh a real feel of competition and i  would challenge anyone who says that  chess is not a sport to come enjoy one  day  of commentary and watching the  competitors and finally i would like to  thank the players without them this  event would have been possible thank you  all very much  you
 

